# Which process can write each fingerprint log string -- decided OFFLINE by grepping the images
# this port ships (2026-09-23). Written for scripts/device/zl1-fingerprint-probe.sh section 4, whose
# comment points here. Host-side and read-only; no device was involved (it is in EDL).

## rule

  A log string can only appear in the log of the process whose address space contains it:
    a vendor library or service in the Android container -> logcat
    a UT-side binary, or a library it dlopens          -> stderr -> the systemd journal of its unit
    a string in NO binary                              -> a count of 0 for it is not evidence
  ONE exception, and it is why two patterns stay logcat-side: a logcat line's TAG is the process
  name, so a daemon that logs under its own name appears without that name being in any binary.

## the images searched

  /mnt/utrootfs          /dev/loop0 /mnt/utrootfs
  /mnt/android-sys-test  /dev/loop7 /mnt/android-sys-test
  /mnt/vendor-ro         /dev/loop9 /mnt/vendor-ro

